# Gitleaks — accepted findings.
#
# Distinct from .gitleaks.toml on purpose. That file allowlists values that were
# NEVER credentials: test fixtures, vendor EXAMPLE keys, documentation
# placeholders. This file records findings that WERE real credentials and are
# accepted as no longer exploitable, each with the evidence that makes it so.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# An entry here only silences the scanner. It does NOT purge the history: the
# value stays readable to anyone who can clone the repo. Part B of
# tasks/secret-rotation-runbook.md is the only thing that removes it for real.
#
# A green Gitleaks run is NOT proof the history is clean.
#
# Re-measured 2026-09-04, by execution rather than by recollection. The previous
# text here said the Deliveroo client_secret was "present in 18 commits". That
# was wrong, and wrong in the direction that matters:
#
#   - 137 commits across all local refs contain it
#   -  41 of those are ancestors of `main`, i.e. published
#   -  96 are local-only, on the pre-monorepo lineage this clone still keeps
#      under `archive/main-avant-monorepo` and 34 stale local tags
#
# The 18 figure counted `apps/restaurant-theme/e2e/deliveroo/test-config.ts`
# alone and silently omitted `scripts/deliveroo-menu-scenarios.sh`, which is
# where the secret actually lived longest. Understated by a factor of 2.3
# against published history, 7.6 against this clone.
#
# Two further figures below were stale and have been corrected in place: the
# scan covered 699 reachable commits (not 492), and the open-PR queue that
# blocked the history rewrite is now EMPTY (not 14) — so the reason Part B was
# deferred no longer holds.
#
# Also corrected: `c0f09cb` is reachable from 35 LOCAL refs and from ZERO remote
# refs, so the claim that CI's checkout fetches it is not true today.
#
# The Deliveroo secret has never had a fingerprint entry in this file. It was
# not suppressed — it was simply never detected, because no rule matched a bare
# 52-character base36 token. Two rules now do: see `.gitleaks.toml`. Once a
# scan runs with them, this file will need a decision on the finding rather
# than continuing to be silent about it.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

